ed for the skipped resend of the legacy event.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:24:- **AC-2.1**: The adapter implements all seven `DerivationProvider` operations over the injected function. Domain handlers are untouched: the same handler code runs against the deterministic provider and the adapter.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:33:  - with a scripted fake function returning distinct canned text per kind, drain a seeded thread and assert all seven `FormKind`s land `ready`\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:35:  - handler equivalence: the same seeded thread drained under the deterministic provider lands the same form rows, states, and subjects with marker content\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:38:  - deterministic-provider forms carry no provenance\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:46:  - fake function returns `{ ok: true, text: \"  \" }`, then success; first attempt classifies `empty_output` retryable and retry lands `ready`\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:64:- It is tempting to pass tests by mocking internal helpers or parsing model text; staged red/green keeps the actual adapter boundary visible.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:101:| TC-2.1 | `test/inference-adapter.test.ts` | seven kinds ready with canned content, handler equivalence, record-authored facts, provenance, deterministic provider without provenance |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:110:| Source/derived provenance authored from output | `test/inference-adapter.test.ts` metadata assertions | Provenance equals assignment provider/model/prompt and deterministic provider has none | Model text could accidentally contain plausible provenance strings |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:172:- Do not create prompt placeholders without golden coverage.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:179:- Evidence: handler-equivalence leg proves unchanged handlers run under deterministic provider and adapter; adapter tests prove drained forms receive real-adapter content and provenance.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:198:- Ready real-adapter forms carry config-stamped provenance; deterministic-provider forms do not.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/01-cli-retirement.md:37:  - constructing with neither `provider` nor `inference` returns the XOR `TypeError`; no fallback resolution path catches it\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/01-cli-retirement.md:46:The SDK remains the product surface. The deterministic provider stays because it is the CI-default fixture provider; only the CLI-only arrival path is removed.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/01-cli-retirement.md:124:- Do not leave a hidden `bin`, wrapper command, registry adapter, or env fallback behind.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:6:Add the opt-in OpenRouter-backed suite with visible ran/not-ran accounting and the real-adapter lifecycle capstone.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:15:**Scope In:** Test-owned OpenRouter `ModelCall`, suite guard, ran/not-ran output, seven real round-trips, shared seam-conformance assertions, and lifecycle capstone structural checks.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:24:- **AC-4.1**: The real-inference suite is opt-in on key presence and its outcome is always visible: ran (with the model assignments used) or not-ran (with reason) in the suite output. Absence of the key can never produce a silent pass. The suite's model-call function lives in test code, implements the AC-1.2 contract, and reaches a real endpoint.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:25:- **AC-4.2**: The capstone: the Epic 04 lifecycle sequence with the real adapter completes with every derivation kind landing `ready` at least once — non-empty content, no deterministic-marker strings, provenance naming the real model — and the deterministic leg's checkpoint-coherence assertions hold structurally (cleared-then-ready around mutations; second compact reflects post-edit content).\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:30:  - with `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY`, each of the seven kinds round-trips real inference once\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:31:  - each result lands `ready`, has non-empty content, and contains no deterministic marker pattern\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:38:  - no deterministic marker pattern appears anywhere\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:45:  - `assertRoutingThroughSdk(openRouterCall, realAssignments)` runs the same routing helper used by Story 2's fake-host seam test, unchanged\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:52:This story proves the same `ModelCall` seam against a real endpoint without making CI depend on network credentials. The OpenRouter function is test-owned host code, not production LHC transport code, and exists to prove that the injected-function contract is sufficient.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:98:| TC-4.3 | `test/inference-real.test.ts` | OpenRouter host passes shared `ModelCall` contract and SDK routing helpers |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:104:| Silent real-suite skip | `test/inference-real.test.ts` unkeyed guard leg | Not-ran record has reason and cannot look like pass | A skipped keyed suite could leave default CI green without proving anything |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:105:| Fixture does not represent host boundary | `test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts` helpers | Same contract/routing helpers run against fake and real host functions | A direct OpenRouter call could pass while violating the SDK boundary shape |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:127:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY` | opt-in suite only | suite reports ran or not-ran |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:128:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL` | opt-in suite optional | fixture default used when unset |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:135:| `test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts` | `createOpenRouterCall(key, defaultModel)` implements `ModelCall` over OpenRouter using plain `fetch` |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:139:OpenRouter failure mapping:\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:153:- `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY` controls keyed execution.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:154:- `LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL` may select the cheap model; fixture default applies when unset.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:155:- OpenRouter provider/model interpretation is host-side and still returns the AC-1.2 `ModelCallResult` shape.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:159:- Do not use deterministic provider output in the real-suite ready assertions.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:160:- Do not hide missing key with test skip semantics indistinguishable from pass.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:161:- Do not mock `fetch` in the keyed leg; the point is real endpoint proof.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:167:- Registration/default path: env-gated suite in default runner reports ran/not-ran; keyed execution reaches OpenRouter through plain `fetch`.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:183:- OpenRouter-backed test `ModelCall` fixture exists and conforms to AC-1.2.\nsrc/inference/adapter.ts:2:// DerivationProvider interface the deterministic provider implements, so\ntest/view-compact.test.ts:42:// deterministic token costs via the literal selection rules — ruling 013;\ntest/view-compact.test.ts:202:    expect(receipt.value.sweep).not.toEqual({ skipped: true });\ntest/view-compact.test.ts:513:describe(\"TC-2.3 (AC-2.5, AC-2.7) + TC-2.5 view-health legs: degraded material renders fallbacks, never fails the compact\", () => {\ntest/view-compact.test.ts:525:  it(\"completes with ladder fallbacks marked, gap entries for unusable spans, and full accounting in the receipt\", async () => {\ntest/view-compact.test.ts:537:    // its ladder (projection pending too) to the deterministic excerpt.\ntest/mutations-delete.test.ts:144:// the deterministic double — the TC-3.6 pattern for exact chunk membership.\ntest/mutations-delete.test.ts:469:    // Reads skip the empty chunk without error: it lists with zero members\ntest/derivation-messages.test.ts:13:  deterministicText,\ntest/derivation-messages.test.ts:89:  it(\"intake a prompt, drain → smoothed form ready with the double's deterministic output\", async () => {\ntest/derivation-messages.test.ts:120:        content: deterministicText(\"smoothPrompt\", { text }, text),\ntest/derivation-messages.test.ts:129:    expect(raw?.content).toBe(deterministicText(\"smoothPrompt\", { text }, text));\ntest/report-repair.test.ts:216:    // deterministically: the failed attempt re-queues with eligible_at past\ntest/report-repair.test.ts:356:    // lets the deterministic id insert below without collision.\ntest/retirement.test.ts:30:  \"deterministicOutcomesSuffix\",\ntest/retirement.test.ts:31:  \"deterministicReceiptsSuffix\",\ntest/retirement.test.ts:32:  \"deterministicText\",\ntest/retirement.test.ts:114:  it(\"neither provider nor inference is the XOR TypeError; no fallback resolution catches it\", () => {\ntest/retirement.test.ts:117:    process.env[envKey] = \"deterministic\";\nsrc/scheduler.ts:121:      // skip — failed_terminal with the stable code, form (if resolvable\nsrc/shared/derivation.ts:53:  gaps?: DependencyGap[]; // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\nsrc/shared/derivation.ts:82:  // from model output. The deterministic provider never sets it.\nsrc/shared/derivation.ts:131:  text: string; // ready form content, or raw/truncated fallback\nsrc/shared/derivation.ts:132:  fallback: boolean; // true ⇒ gap recorded\nsrc/shared/derivation.ts:176:// unchanged — the deterministic test default) or `inference` (host\ntest/inference-classification.test.ts:144:        { ok: false, kind: \"rate_limit\", message: \"throttled by the fake host\" },\ntest/inference-classification.test.ts:145:        { ok: false, kind: \"rate_limit\", message: \"throttled by the fake host\" },\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:10:Four epics built a derivation pipeline that has never made a model call. The seam was designed for this moment: `DerivationProvider` is an interface with seven semantic operations, the deterministic provider implements it with marker strings, and every handler, queue row, retry path, and state transition in `domains/` is provider-agnostic. This epic builds the second implementation of that interface — the real one — plus the injection path that lets a host supply model access without LHC ever touching a credential.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:21:- **DD-2: The adapter is a `DerivationProvider`.** No seam movement. `createInferenceProvider(inference, config)` returns the same interface the deterministic provider implements; `createSdk` and everything below it see a provider, full stop. Handlers, queue, drain, states: zero changes for Flows 1–4 (except the one-line provenance copy, DD-4).\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:23:- **DD-4: Provenance rides the `ProviderResult` and is copied, never authored.** The ok branch gains `provenance?: { provider, model, prompt }`. The adapter stamps it (it alone knows the assignment); handlers copy it into `DerivedFormMetadata.provenance` alongside the existing mechanical stamps. The deterministic provider simply never sets it. This keeps the \"metadata is mechanically stamped\" invariant: provenance comes from config-known strings, not model output.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:24:- **DD-5: Construction is `provider` XOR `inference`.** `createSdk` accepts exactly one. The `inference` path validates the assignment map (all seven `FormKind`s present, every prompt name known) and builds the adapter; the `provider` path is unchanged and keeps the deterministic provider as the test default. Both/neither is a `TypeError` at construction, matching the existing config-mistakes-throw contract.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:31:- **DD-12: CLI deletion removes the registry, keeps the deterministic provider.** `src/providers/registry.ts` (named resolution, `LHC_PROVIDER`) dies with its only consumer. `src/providers/deterministic.ts` stays — it is the CI-default test provider and the byte-stable fixture substrate. The twelve `cli-process-*.test.ts` suites delete; `verify-all` drops the `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE` gate and gains the opt-in inference suite (which self-reports ran/not-ran).\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:32:- **DD-13: The real-inference suite is a second host of the same contract.** The OpenRouter-backed `ModelCall` lives in `test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts`, implements the AC-1.2 contract over plain `fetch`, and runs Flow 1's construction/routing assertions parameterized (question 5, resolved: shared assertion helpers parameterized over the function, not duplicated tests). Key arrives via `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY`; absence produces an explicit not-ran record, never a silent pass.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:79:│   ├── deterministic.ts                # EXISTS: unchanged — CI-default test provider\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:98:| `test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts` | NEW (test) | The real `ModelCall` host: fetch to OpenRouter, contract-conformant failures, key resolution | — | AC-4.1 |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:149:What the adapter must never do: parse the response for outcomes, receipts, or any mechanical fact. Those stamps happen in handlers from the record, exactly as under the deterministic provider (AC-2.2). The adapter's only additions to the result are the text and the config-known provenance strings.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:171:The suite (`test/inference-real.test.ts`) keys on `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY`. Present: build the OpenRouter `ModelCall` fixture, construct an SDK with all seven kinds assigned to the configured cheap model (`LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL`, defaulted in the fixture), and run the legs. Absent: emit one structured not-ran record (a test that asserts-and-reports the skip reason loudly — visible in output as `NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)`, never a green checkmark indistinguishable from a pass). The accounting rule is implemented as a suite-level guard, not per-test `skip`s, so the run/not-run state is one fact reported once.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:173:The capstone reuses Epic 04's lifecycle sequence with the assertion set swapped: where the deterministic leg asserted byte-exact replay and marker content, this leg asserts structure — every `FormKind` reaches `ready` at least once with non-empty text containing no deterministic marker pattern (`/^(smoothed|toolcall|toolresult|rendering|projection|detailed|brief)\\(/`), provenance naming the real model, and the checkpoint-coherence ladder (mutation clears → pending; drain → ready with *different* content; second compact's view reflects post-edit content).\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:262:/** The real provider. Same interface the deterministic provider implements;\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:298:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY` | Opt-in suite only | Suite self-reports ran/not-ran; never required by CI default |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:299:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL` | Opt-in suite, optional | Fixture default (cheap model) used when unset |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:301:No new dependencies. The OpenRouter fixture uses plain `fetch` in test code (epic NFR).\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:305:The mock boundary moves with this epic, and naming it precisely is the design's most important testing statement: **the external boundary is now the `ModelCall` function.** Flows 1–3 test against scripted fake functions (canned successes, scripted failure sequences, recording wrappers) — these are boundary mocks, not internal mocks, because the function *is* where LHC's code ends. The `DerivationProvider` interface is no longer the mock seam for this epic's tests; it's internal wiring under test (the adapter is the unit). Epic 02–04 suites keep their provider-level doubles untouched — their subject was never the adapter.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:307:Everything else follows house rules: real temp SQLite for anything touching thread state (boundary tests, capstone), no internal module mocks, deterministic provider remains the CI default for all existing suites. The opt-in suite is the only network-touching code in the repo and is labeled in `verify-all` accounting as `ran` or `not-ran (reason)` — the four-tier verify scripts keep their names; composition changes are in Flow 6.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:317:| 0: Foundation | `inference/types.ts`, provenance type additions, fake-call fixtures (`test/fixtures/model-call.ts`: recording/scripted builders), prompt-template type + registry skeleton | — | Fixture validity: scripted fakes must satisfy the AC-1.2 contract shape |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:322:| 5: Real suite + capstone | OpenRouter fixture, accounting guard, seven round-trips, capstone leg | 4.1–4.2 | Silent skip (the accounting guard is the deliverable; review it first) |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:332:| Config generalization (token-band routing, fallback chains) | Flow 1 | Vocabulary derived from seven dialed-in answers | Post-dial-in design |\ntest/messages-read.test.ts:45:// deterministic double so m1's smoothing and m3/m4's tool summaries sit\ntest/messages-read.test.ts:203:    // Anti-shim: the forms ARE the owner report's entries for this message,\ntest/projection.test.ts:241:  it(\"TC-5.4 (message clause): a skipped event creates no duplicate message (AC-5.4)\", async () => {\ntest/projection.test.ts:252:    expect(resend.value.events.every((entry) => entry.outcome === \"skipped\")).toBe(true);\ntest/inference-prompts.test.ts:7:// operations, never the renderers alone (anti-shim).\ntest/inference-prompts.test.ts:56:        { messageId: \"m1\", kind: \"user_prompt\", text: \"please read notes/plan.md\", fallback: false },\ntest/inference-prompts.test.ts:61:          fallback: false,\ntest/inference-prompts.test.ts:64:        { messageId: \"m3\", kind: \"a