 → `auth`, 429 → `rate_limit`, 400 → `invalid_request`, network errors → `network`, everything else → `other`, and extracts non-empty assistant text into the `ModelCallResult` success shape. `resolveRealSuiteEnv()` → `{ key, model } | { notRan: reason }`.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:289:- handler equivalence: the same seeded thread drained under the deterministic provider lands the same form rows (states, subjects) with marker content — proving handlers unchanged (AC-2.1)\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:291:- each form's `metadata.provenance` equals its assignment `{ provider, model, prompt }`; deterministic-provider forms carry none\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:331:- `assertModelCallContract(openRouterCall)` and `assertRoutingThroughSdk(openRouterCall, realAssignments)` — the same helpers TC-1.2 ran against the fake, unchanged (DD-13)\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:363:- constructing with neither `provider` nor `inference` → the XOR `TypeError` (no fallback resolution path exists to catch it)\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:377:Lifecycle/capstone deterministic legs (Epic 04's exercise) are untouched: they run the deterministic provider and never asserted boundary trigger timing.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:390:| 5: Real suite | `inference-real` (guard testable unkeyed) | OpenRouter fixture, accounting guard, capstone leg | unkeyed: not-ran record asserted in CI; keyed: TC-4.1–4.3 green locally (run recorded in story DoD with model used) |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:393:**Story-completion accounting for Chunk 5:** the keyed run cannot gate CI (no secret in CI by design). The story's DoD requires a recorded keyed run — date, model, pass state — in the deviation/completion notes. A keyed run that has never happened blocks epic acceptance: the capstone is the integration-readiness gate, and an unexercised gate is the silent-skip failure mode this suite exists to prevent.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:403:| Silent real-suite skip | TC-4.1's unkeyed leg asserts the not-ran record exists and is not a pass |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:447:    planSummary: \"Implemented the Story 3 adapter pipeline behind the unchanged Epic 02 seam: each operation now bounds input where DD-7 applies (summarizeToolResult head+tail+marker under maxInputChars), renders its kind's prompt, calls the host ModelCall, rejects empty/whitespace-only success text as retryable empty_output, and returns trimmed text with config-stamped provenance. Ported the POC's settled smoothing prompt verbatim into smoothing-v1 (the other six templates remain marked pre-dial-in with golden coverage). Handlers copy result.provenance into DerivedFormMetadata at all five form-write sites (messages landForm; turns rendering/projection/chunk-summary); the deterministic provider sets none, so its forms carry none. Wrote prompt goldens for all seven templates plus the two story suites covering TC-2.1, TC-2.2, and TC-2.3, demonstrated red on the new behaviors before implementing, and recorded the new Red files in the immutability manifest.\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:454:        reason: \"Replaced the pre-dial-in placeholder with the POC's settled smoothing system prompt, ported verbatim (AC-2.3)\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:463:        reason: \"TC-2.1 and TC-2.3: seven kinds ready with canned content and assignment provenance, record-authored outcomes/receipts disagreeing with adversarial canned text, handler equivalence under the deterministic provider with no provenance, empty-output retry/exhaustion/shaping legs\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/005-story-orchestrate-resume.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate resume\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"result\":{\"case\":\"completed\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"storyId\":\"01-cli-retirement\",\"storyRunId\":\"01-cli-retirement-story-run-001\",\"currentSnapshotPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"eventHistoryPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\",\"finalPackagePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/story-lead/001-final-package.json\",\"finalPackage\":{\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"storyRunId\":\"01-cli-retirement-story-run-001\",\"storyId\":\"01-cli-retirement\",\"attempt\":1,\"summary\":{\"storyTitle\":\"Story 1: CLI Retirement\",\"implementedScope\":\"Deletion-first CLI retirement per Flow 6 / DD-12. Deleted src/cli/ (8 modules), the src/cli.ts bin entrypoint, the named-provider registry (src/providers/registry.ts), the package bin entry and dev:cli script, and all twelve spawned cli-process-*.test.ts suites. src/index.ts now re-exports sdk.js only (runCli/CliResult gone); sdk.ts dropped the registry re-exports and gained the XOR construction error ('createSdk config: exactly one of provider or inference') ahead of all other validation, so the neither-provider-nor-inference case names the final contract with no fallback path. Verify scripts lost the LHC_PROCESS_SUITE gate and the SKIP echo; vitest.config.ts collapsed to one default no-network tier. Beyond the twelve spawned suites, the in-process CLI parity legs embedded in nine default-suite files (and the twinThreads parity fixture) were removed surgically — every SDK behavior assertion they accompanied was retained, verified by before/after suite comparison (328 default tests -> 309 = 25 parity-only legs removed + 6 new retirement tests). test/retirement.test.ts proves the SDK-only export snapshot, no bin manifest, deleted-surface absence, zero LHC_PROVIDER/--provider references under src/, and the XOR TypeError surviving a set LHC_PROVIDER env var. Red-manifest regenerated for amended/deleted/added test files.\",\"acceptanceRationale\":\"Story-lead is pausing for caller ruling 01-cli-retirement-story-run-001-ruling-spec-deviation before impl-lead can accept the story.\"},\"evidence\":{\"implementorArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/006-implementor.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"selfReviewArtifacts\":[],\"verifierArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/007-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"quickFixArtifacts\":[],\"callerInputArtifacts\":[],\"gateRuns\":[{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && node scripts/check-test-immutability.mjs\",\"result\":\"pass\"}]},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"pass\",\"findings\":[]},\"riskAndDeviationReview\":{\"specDeviations\":[{\"description\":\"Epic 04 parity-gap note (required by DoD): spawned `inspect health` parity was backfilled before Epic 05 (cli-process-inspect.test.ts), and this story deletes the spawned-process parity surface instead of carrying it forward.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/006-implementor.json\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"needs-ruling\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"SdkConfig keeps `provider` as a required typed field this story; the runtime XOR TypeError ('createSdk config: exactly one of provider or inference') is in place per TC-6.2, but the typed `provider?`/`inference?` reshape needs InferenceConfig and lands in Story 2 per the chunk dependency order (0 -> 2). The retirement test exercises the runtime contract via an unknown-shape cast.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/006-implementor.json\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"needs-ruling\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"Removed two CLI-only ErrorCode union members (`empty_stdin`, `provider_not_configured`) beyond the named export deletions — their only consumers were the deleted CLI adapter and process suites; leaving them would be dead resolution vocabulary contrary to the anti-shim requirements.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/006-implementor.js