tone leg | unkeyed: not-ran record asserted in CI; keyed: TC-4.1–4.3 green locally (run recorded in story DoD with model used) |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:393:**Story-completion accounting for Chunk 5:** the keyed run cannot gate CI (no secret in CI by design). The story's DoD requires a recorded keyed run — date, model, pass state — in the deviation/completion notes. A keyed run that has never happened blocks epic acceptance: the capstone is the integration-readiness gate, and an unexercised gate is the silent-skip failure mode this suite exists to prevent.\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:403:| Silent real-suite skip | TC-4.1's unkeyed leg asserts the not-ran record exists and is not a pass |\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:490:      - \"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real production execution path was introduced in the touched inference adapter path.\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:530:    planSummary: \"Implemented the Story 3 adapter pipeline behind the unchanged Epic 02 seam: each operation now bounds input where DD-7 applies (summarizeToolResult head+tail+marker under maxInputChars), renders its kind's prompt, calls the host ModelCall, rejects empty/whitespace-only success text as retryable empty_output, and returns trimmed text with config-stamped provenance. Ported the POC's settled smoothing prompt verbatim into smoothing-v1 (the other six templates remain marked pre-dial-in with golden coverage). Handlers copy result.provenance into DerivedFormMetadata at all five form-write sites (messages landForm; turns rendering/projection/chunk-summary); the deterministic provider sets none, so its forms carry none. Wrote prompt goldens for all seven templates plus the two story suites covering TC-2.1, TC-2.2, and TC-2.3, demonstrated red on the new behaviors before implementing, and recorded the new Red files in the immutability manifest.\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:537:        reason: \"Replaced the pre-dial-in placeholder with the POC's settled smoothing system prompt, ported verbatim (AC-2.3)\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:546:        reason: \"TC-2.1 and TC-2.3: seven kinds ready with canned content and assignment provenance, record-authored outcomes/receipts disagreeing with adversarial canned text, handler equivalence under the deterministic provider with no provenance, empty-output retry/exhaustion/shaping legs\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:713:        - \"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: all seven DerivationProvider operations exist on the adapter, seeded drains land all seven kinds ready, and deterministic-provider handler equivalence is covered by inference-adapter.test.ts.\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:717:        - \"AC-2.5 / TC-2.1: ready adapter forms carry assignment-stamped provider/model/prompt provenance, and deterministic-provider forms carry no provenance.\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:738:      - \"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or mock path was found in production inference code; test fakes are confined to test fixtures.\"\ndocs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/pr